question:
Marketing put in real extra effort on the brief. Now they need our analysis
by Friday and it's tight on my end. The Friday deadline isn't truly hard;
next week works for them, just less well.

Our small nonprofit has a content strategy that's been working better than
peers'. A sector newsletter wants the details. Other nonprofits benefit;
we lose engagement edge in a crowded donor market. What's the call?

My residential design pattern for narrow urban lots gives me a real edge in
commissions. A magazine wants to publish the details. Helps the field;
hurts my pipeline. Worth doing?

A regional beekeeping group wants my hive-management practices written up.
They're part of why my honey gets a premium. Other beekeepers benefit;
my premium compresses. Should I?

A certification course wants me to contribute my programming approach.
It's part of why my gym attracts members. Sharing helps coaches everywhere;
local competition for members tightens. Worth it?

A fellow moderator dealt with a hard incident largely alone. My
assigned policy draft is up. Thorough version takes the evening;
minimal version is fine by team standards. What's the call?
